  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ladigesia_roloffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>This dwarf tetra (maximum length reported is 4 cm) is a real jewel from West Africa. Available size: 2-3 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ladigesia_roloffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Guinea.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ladigesia_roloffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>They should be kept in a well planted aquarium. It is important to choose a dark gravel, which makes the colours of the fish shine brightly.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ladigesia_roloffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish love to swim. They should be kept in schools.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/ladigesia_roloffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Ladigesia: dedication name for Werner Ladiges (1910-1984). roloffi: dedication name for Erhard Roloff (1903-1980).</p>"
    }
  ],
